Source: jvc
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: mplx <jennifer@mplx.dev>
Homepage: https://github.com/jennifer-language/jvc
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/jennifer-language/jvc
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/jennifer-language/jvc.git
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: jvc
Architecture: all
Depends: jennifer (>= @ENGINE_FLOOR@)
Recommends: git
Description: deck manager for the Jennifer programming language
 jvc resolves, vendors, and publishes Jennifer decks, the way composer
 does for PHP or cargo does for Rust. It reads a deck.toml, resolves the
 whole dependency graph against a deck repository, and pins the result in
 a camcorder.lock so that a fresh checkout plus `jvc install` reproduces
 the same code.
 .
 The package is architecture-independent Jennifer source: the launcher at
 /usr/bin/jvc is a symlink into /usr/share/jvc, where bin/ and src/ sit
 side by side because the launcher reaches its modules through a relative
 import.
 .
 The versioned dependency on jennifer is the compatibility contract. It
 mirrors the [engines] table in jvc's own deck.toml, and the interpreter
 enforces the same floor at read time from the
 `# pragma-jennifer-version:` header each source file carries.
 .
 git is a recommendation rather than a dependency because the common path
 does not need it: installing decks from a repository uses HTTP only. git
 is required for decks resolved from a [sources] git remote, for
 `jvc app install`, and for publishing, which reads the tag and remote of
 the working tree.
